{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And the sons of Israel came, etc., for the famine was, etc.</b> It was necessary to restate <b>for the famine was</b> etc. The verse intends to give a reason for those who were coming, so that you should not say: where were the comers mentioned as being among them? Therefore it says כִּי הָיָה etc., and there are those who came." "Further, the verse intends to say that they took pains to hide themselves, and came mingled among the others who came to buy grain, because the famine was in the land of Canaan — for in this way they would not fall under suspicion of espionage, which was Joseph's suspicion of them. And this is the verse's measure: <b>and the sons of Israel came</b>, and the manner of their coming was among the comers — their coming being <b>for the famine was</b> etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:52.168210067Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}